{
  "$schema_version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "description": "Normalized domain.operation view of datasets/intents.json for brain/router (hybrid semantic router). This file does NOT replace datasets/intents.json — it is a deliberate projection of a subset of it (only intents whose response_mode is 'skill' AND that are not already handled by a deterministic guard in brain/intent_engine.py). Conversational intents (smalltalk, identity, joke, motivate, opinion, followup, general_query, unknown) and guard-handled intents (dismissal, greet, farewell, thanks, help, perform_action) are intentionally excluded — they keep using their existing paths. Each operation's 'seeds' list holds its semantic prototypes: one stored vector per seed, aggregated per domain.operation at retrieval time. Add prototypes here, never in routing code; the same seed may not appear under two operations. If datasets/intents.json's keyword_rules_order, an intent id, or an intent's response_mode changes, this file must be reviewed for drift; brain/router/command_vector_store.py fingerprints this file (not datasets/intents.json) to decide when to reseed."
  },
